<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Langensalza (1075)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1075</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Homburg on the Unstrut</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Langensalza, also called the Battle of Homburg on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unstrut">Unstrut</a>, was fought on 9 June 1075 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> rebellion against the Salian king Henry IV. Henry defeated the rebel Saxon nobility, whose leaders submitted to him later that year. The Saxon opposition revived soon afterwards during the Investiture Controversy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-langensalza-1075.jpg" alt="Battle of Langensalza (1075)" width="320" height="568" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Otakar Frankenberger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plan_of_the_attack_during_the_battle_of_Langensalza_(Homburg,_1075).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
